  "title": "Sliding Window Median",
  "language": "python",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "source": "LeetCode #480 variant with float output",
  "description": "Write a Python function `median_sliding_window(nums: list[int], k: int) -> list[float]` that returns the median of each sliding window of size `k` as a list of floats.\n\nFor a window of odd size `k`, the median is the middle element when sorted.\nFor a window of even size `k`, the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n\nFunction signature:\ndef median_sliding_window(nums: list[int], k: int) -> list[float]:",
  "function_signature": "def median_sliding_window(nums: list[int], k: int) -> list[float]:",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= k <= len(nums) <= 10^5",
    "-2^31 <= nums[i] <= 2^31 - 1",
    "Output values are floats (use exact arithmetic \u2014 no rounding)"
  ],
